cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AuditLane, please cite it as below."
title: "AuditLane: A Reproducible Pre-Audit Cleanroom for the Arbitrum Audit Program"
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Dipankar
year: 2026
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/doom2quake/auditlane"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doom2quake/auditlane"
abstract: >-
  AuditLane is a reproducible pre-audit cleanroom for Arbitrum projects entering
  the Arbitrum Audit Program. It folds a target repo into a single content-addressed
  manifest: a pinned toolchain, captured test counts, and every contract's source
  hash and Arbitrum Sepolia deployed-bytecode hash checked against the built
  artifact. The manifest is a pure function of the repo state, so a reviewer re-runs
  the same command and gets a byte-for-byte identical manifest id, and a deployed
  bytecode that does not match the artifact fails the package closed with a fixed
  reason code. The same seven reason codes and their order are recomputed on-chain in
  BuildRegistry.sol, so a whitelisted audit firm never has to trust the tool's word
  for the verdict. Milestone 1: the cleanroom core and the on-chain reference,
  verified with pytest and forge. Arbitrum Sepolia testnet only.
